# NOTE: Assertions have been autogenerated by utils/update_mir_test_checks.py UTC_ARGS: --version 5
# Crash when aggressive realloc de-allocates a register that is live-through an
# empty loop, and a subsequent loop defines that same register with a
# high-latency instruction: getHighOutputLatencyRegs then calls VRM->getPhys()
# on the now-unmapped VReg and feeds NoRegister to MCRegAliasIterator.
#
# %2 and %3 are live-through bb.1, which has no renaming candidates, so nothing
# re-assigns them before bb.3 is processed. %3 is defined in bb.3 by a mayLoad
# instruction, which is what triggers the unguarded lookup.
#
